{"title":"Blockchain Developer Roadmap","role":"Blockchain Developer","summary":"A Blockchain Developer designs, develops, tests, and deploys decentralized applications and blockchain-based systems. The role combines:","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"CSE - Cyber Security & IoT incl. Blockchain"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Blockchain Developer designs, develops, tests, and deploys decentralized applications and blockchain-based systems. The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Programming and software engineering"},{"text":"Blockchain architecture"},{"text":"Smart contract development"},{"text":"Cryptography fundamentals"},{"text":"Distributed systems"},{"text":"Web3 application development"},{"text":"Backend/API development"},{"text":"Wallet and blockchain integration"},{"text":"Cybersecurity"},{"text":"Cloud and DevOps"},{"text":"A strong graduate should be able to build both smart contracts and the applications that interact with them."}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech – CSE Cyber Security / IoT / Blockchain","Blockchain Developer / Web3 Developer","Smart Contract Developer / Blockchain Engineer","Senior Blockchain Engineer","Blockchain Architect / Protocol Engineer","Web3 Technical Lead / Engineering Manager","Blockchain Platform Architect / CTO"]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Tech","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The ideal skill progression is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Programming","Data Structures & Algorithms","Computer Networks + Operating Systems + DBMS","Cryptography & Cybersecurity","Distributed Systems","Blockchain Fundamentals","Ethereum / EVM","Solidity + Smart Contracts","Web3 Application Development","Testing + Security Auditing","Deployment + Cloud"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Programming & Computer Science Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"Master at least one primary language:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"JavaScript / TypeScript"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Java"},{"text":"C++"},{"text":"For blockchain development, JavaScript/TypeScript + Solidity is particularly valuable."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Core Topics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Variables and data types"},{"text":"Functions"},{"text":"OOP"},{"text":"Exception handling"},{"text":"File handling"},{"text":"APIs"},{"text":"Git/GitHub"},{"text":"Debugging"},{"text":"Basic software engineering"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data Structures & Algorithms"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arrays"},{"text":"Strings"},{"text":"Linked lists"},{"text":"Stacks"},{"text":"Queues"},{"text":"Hash tables"},{"text":"Trees"},{"text":"Graphs"},{"text":"Heaps"},{"text":"Sorting"},{"text":"Searching"},{"text":"Recursion"},{"text":"Dynamic programming"},{"text":"Complexity analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1–2 — Core Computer Science"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong fundamentals in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Operating Systems"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Processes"},{"text":"Threads"},{"text":"Memory management"},{"text":"File systems"},{"text":"Concurrency"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Computer Networks"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"TCP/IP"},{"text":"HTTP/HTTPS"},{"text":"DNS"},{"text":"REST APIs"},{"text":"WebSockets"},{"text":"Network security"},{"text":"Peer-to-peer networking"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Database Systems"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"PostgreSQL/MySQL"},{"text":"NoSQL concepts"},{"text":"Database indexing"},{"text":"Transactions"},{"text":"ACID properties"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Software Engineering"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Git/GitHub"},{"text":"Linux"},{"text":"Testing"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Design patterns"},{"text":"CI/CD fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Cryptography & Cybersecurity"},{"type":"p","text":"Because the specialization includes Cyber Security, students should develop a strong security foundation."},{"type":"h","text":"Cryptography"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hash functions"},{"text":"SHA-256"},{"text":"Public/private key cryptography"},{"text":"Digital signatures"},{"text":"RSA"},{"text":"Elliptic Curve Cryptography"},{"text":"Key management"},{"text":"Message authentication"},{"text":"Merkle trees"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Blockchain-Relevant Cryptography"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Private Key","Digital Signature","Transaction Authentication","Blockchain Network","Consensus"]},{"type":"p","text":"Also learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Wallet addresses"},{"text":"Seed phrases"},{"text":"Public/private key relationships"},{"text":"Transaction signing"},{"text":"Hash-linked data structures"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Blockchain Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand blockchain from the protocol level before learning frameworks."},{"type":"h","text":"Core Concepts"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Blocks"},{"text":"Transactions"},{"text":"Nodes"},{"text":"Distributed ledgers"},{"text":"Peer-to-peer networks"},{"text":"Consensus mechanisms"},{"text":"Mining"},{"text":"Validators"},{"text":"Smart contracts"},{"text":"Wallets"},{"text":"Gas"},{"text":"Tokens"},{"text":"Forks"},{"text":"Block explorers"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Consensus"},{"type":"p","text":"Study the concepts behind:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Proof of Work"},{"text":"Proof of Stake"},{"text":"Delegated mechanisms"},{"text":"Byzantine Fault Tolerance"},{"text":"Understand why consensus is required, not just how to use a blockchain."}]}]},{"heading":"Ethereum & EVM","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Ethereum is an important ecosystem for blockchain developers."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ethereum architecture"},{"text":"EVM"},{"text":"Accounts"},{"text":"Transactions"},{"text":"Gas"},{"text":"Blocks"},{"text":"Nodes"},{"text":"RPC"},{"text":"Smart contracts"},{"text":"Events"},{"text":"Logs"},{"text":"ABI"},{"text":"Ethereum-compatible networks"},{"text":"Layer-2 concepts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the relationship:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Frontend","Web3 Library","Wallet","RPC Provider","Blockchain Network","Smart Contract"]}]},{"heading":"Year 2–3 — Solidity & Smart Contracts","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Solidity"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Contract structure"},{"text":"Variables"},{"text":"Functions"},{"text":"Modifiers"},{"text":"Events"},{"text":"Structs"},{"text":"Arrays"},{"text":"Mappings"},{"text":"Inheritance"},{"text":"Interfaces"},{"text":"Libraries"},{"text":"Access control"},{"text":"Error handling"},{"text":"Payable functions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Solidity"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Contract composition"},{"text":"Upgradeable contracts"},{"text":"Proxy patterns"},{"text":"Gas optimization"},{"text":"Storage layout"},{"text":"Contract interactions"},{"text":"Token standards"}]}]},{"heading":"Token Standards","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand commonly used standards and their purposes:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ERC-20 — fungible tokens"},{"text":"ERC-721 — NFTs"},{"text":"ERC-1155 — multi-token standard"},{"text":"ERC-4626 — tokenized vaults"},{"text":"Students should understand how token contracts work rather than simply copying existing contracts."}]}]},{"heading":"Smart Contract Security","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Security is one of the most important skills for a blockchain developer."},{"type":"p","text":"Study vulnerabilities such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Reentrancy"},{"text":"Integer-related vulnerabilities"},{"text":"Access-control flaws"},{"text":"Oracle manipulation"},{"text":"Flash-loan-related attacks"},{"text":"Front-