 graduate beyond basic Web3 application development."}]}]},{"heading":"Target Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong student graduating from this specialization should be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Write production-quality Solidity contracts."},{"text":"Explain blockchain architecture and consensus."},{"text":"Develop and test smart contracts."},{"text":"Build a complete Web3 application."},{"text":"Connect wallets and blockchain networks."},{"text":"Build backend APIs interacting with blockchain systems."},{"text":"Understand cryptographic signatures and hashing."},{"text":"Identify common smart-contract vulnerabilities."},{"text":"Use Git, Linux, Docker and CI/CD."},{"text":"Work with blockchain data and events."},{"text":"Integrate blockchain concepts with IoT systems."},{"text":"Deploy a complete project."},{"text":"Explain architectural trade-offs between on-chain and off-chain systems."},{"text":"Maintain a strong GitHub portfolio with 3–5 substantial blockchain projects."}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For this degree, the strongest career preparation is not simply learning Solidity."},{"type":"p","text":"The ideal profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Blockchain Developer","Software Engineer","Cybersecurity Foundation","Distributed Systems Knowledge"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"A student who combines Solidity, TypeScript, smart-contract security, backend development, cryptography, distributed systems, and cloud deployment will have a substantially stronger foundation for Blockchain Developer and Web3 Engineering roles than someone who only knows basic smart-contract syntax."}]}]}